# xtdl-armor-example: a FICTIONAL format, invented only for this example: a
# `bits` message carried as six-bit armored text (engine-spec 0.14), each
# character six bits, with a call sign in six-bit characters. Layout: pack.md.
format        xtdl-armor-example
version       0.1.0
distribution  controlled
source        "invented for this example; no external document"
uses          xtdl
wire          bits
word_bytes    1
bit_order     msb
armor         sixbit

kind     position
when     0:0:6      9
field    xtdl.sector  0:6:5     uint
field    lat          0:11:28   sscale:1/600000  absent 54600000
field    lon          0:39:29   sscale:1/600000  absent 108600000
field    callsign     0:68:42   sixbit           trim
field    speed_ms     0:110:10  uscale:1/10      optional
